# WolkaraForever layer patch 0067 - host: the world by touch with TouchPlay (iPad touch)
#
# Why: in iPad touch the TouchPlay add-on draws the game's touch buttons and saves them with three
# settings for the rest of the screen (the contract, TouchContract.h): its hold time, whether the
# character turns with the view, and a world key. 0066 gave the buttons their fingers; this is the
# world - a finger no button takes - and the finger that leaves a spell to aim it. With a contract:
#   - A tap is still a left click where the finger is (0055). A second tap within 40 pt and 1.5 s of
#     the last is a right click there instead (talk, loot, attack), and the record is gone. A drag, a
#     hold or a pinch in between also clears it. The time is the areas' clock (fixture-driven in tests).
#   - Kept still for the contract's hold time, the finger sends the world key (the cursor is under it -
#     put back there first if an aimed spell moved it - so the add-on shows the card of what is there)
#     instead of 0055's right click. A world key the reader does not know is 0055's right click.
#   - A drag (past 0055's 10 pt slop) is a right drag when the contract says turn=1 (the character
#     turns with the view), a left drag when turn=0.
#   - A finger that lands within 20 pt of the view's edge posts nothing at all: it is handed to the
#     areas to hold quietly until it lifts, and the pinch never takes it.
#   - A spell dragged off its button (TouchAreas.m) moves the pointer through touchPointerAt:click:,
#     the second method of the areas' key sink: a mouse move with no button down, so the game's circle
#     follows the finger; the lift on the world is a left click there. If another finger is dragging the
#     view, the aim ends that drag first (its button up, as a pinch does). Stopping an aim (a lift over a
#     button, a cancel) is Interact's hold key, the add-on's "stop" button, through 0066's key path -
#     never Escape. A separate world tap while a spell is aimed also places it (the game takes that
#     tap's click).
# With no contract, and in every other interface mode, the host is exactly 0055 + 0065 + 0066.
#
# Applies after: 0066-touchplay-buttons-take-their-fingers.patch
# Applies to: translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
# Upstream: no (TouchPlay and iPad touch live in the WolkaraForever layer).
#
--- a/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
